- Play Forest, then cast Earth King's Lieutenant {G}{W} — 1/1 trample with Ally synergy.\n\
- Play Plains, cast Avatar Enthusiasts {2}{W} — 2/2.\n\
- Play The Spirit Oasis? It costs {2}{U} — it's not a land, it's an artifact (Shrine). Wait, \"The Spirit Oasis {2}{U}: When this enters, draw a card for each Shrine you control.\" It's a Shrine artifact presumably. I can't play it as a land.\n\
\n\
The Choices only show Forest and Plains as land plays — so The Spirit Oasis is a spell (Shrine artifact), not a land.\n\
\n\
Best play: I want to develop my Ally board. With Island + Plains + Forest, I can cast Earth King's Lieutenant ({G}{W}). But it's a 1/1 — weak on its own. Avatar Enthusiasts ({2}{W}) is a 2/2 that grows with each Ally.\n\
\n\
Actually, sequencing thought: Avatar Enthusiasts first, then Lieutenant next turn would put a counter on Enthusiasts when it enters (as another Ally). Also Lieutenant entering puts counters on other Allies.\n\
\n\
Turn 3: Play Forest, cast Earth King's Lieutenant? That leaves a 1/1. Or play Plains, cast Avatar Enthusiasts (2/2). \n\
\n\
Hmm, but consider next turn: turn 4 with 4 lands (Island, Plains, Forest, + land drop). I could cast Hakoda {3}{W} (3/5 vigilance) or Flexible Waterbender {3}{U} (2/5 vigilance), or Earth Kingdom Soldier {4}{G/W} (3/4 vigilance, puts counters on up to two creatures).\n\
\n\
Curve consideration: Turn 3 Avatar Enthusiasts (2/2), turn 4 Earth King's Lieutenant (gets a counter when another Ally enters... wait, Lieutenant's own text: \"Whenever another Ally you control enters, put a +1/+1 counter on this\" — so Lieutenant grows too). When Lieutenant enters with Enthusiasts out: Enthusiasts gets a counter (becomes 3/3), Lieutenant puts a counter on each other Ally (Enthusiasts gets another → 4/4). That's strong.\n\
\n\
Alternatively turn 3 Lieutenant (1/1), turn 4 Enthusiasts: Enthusiasts enters → Lieutenant gets a counter (2/2), Enthusiasts is 2/2. Less explosive.\n\
\n\
So play Avatar Enthusiasts first. To cast it I need {2}{W}: I have Island + Plains untapped, and I'll play Plains as my land drop → Plains + Plains + Island, tap two Plains and... {2}{W} = two generic + white. Tap Island + Plains for the 2 generic? No wait, I need W specifically. Tap Plains for W, Island + other Plains for {2}. That works.\n\
\n\
Actually, should I play Forest instead and cast Lieutenant? Avatar Enthusiasts is the better turn-3 play as established.\n\
\n\
Hmm, but what about mana next turn? If I play Plains now: board = Island, Plains, Plains. Next turn land drop → Forest (from hand) gives me G, W, U — all colors, 4 mana. Can cast Hakoda ({3}{W}) or Waterbender ({3}{U}) or Lieutenant ({G}{W}).\n\
\n\
If I play Forest now: Island, Plains, Forest — casts Lieutenant. Next turn play Plains → can cast Hakoda/Waterbender/Soldier.\n\
\n\
I think Enthusiasts first is better for the Ally curve. Play Plains, cast Avatar Enthusiasts.\n\
\n\
