      "thinking": "Let me look at the situation. It's turn 3, postcombat main. I have Island, Plains, Plains on the battlefield. My hand: Avatar Enthusiasts, Earth King's Lieutenant, Earth Kingdom Soldier, Flexible Waterbender, Forest, Hakoda, Selfless Commander, The Spirit Oasis.\n\
\n\
Wait, the game log says I played Plains and cast Avatar Enthusiasts on turn 3... but the board shows Avatar Enthusiasts still in hand. Hmm, the summary said \"I'm playing Plains to double up on white, then casting Avatar Enthusiasts\" — but the board shows 3 lands (Island, Plains, Plains) and Avatar Enthusiasts still in hand. Maybe the earlier action didn't happen yet, or the recap was aspirational. Anyway, now I have 3 mana and can cast Avatar Enthusiasts {2}{W}.\n\
\n\
Choices: Avatar Enthusiasts or The Spirit Oasis {2}{U}. Spirit Oasis draws a card for each Shrine I control when it enters — I control no Shrines, so it draws 0. That's not great. Avatar Enthusiasts is a 2/2 that grows with Allies. I should cast Avatar Enthusiasts.\n\
\n\
Note Earth King's Lieutenant needs {G}{W} — I have Forest in hand, so next turn I can play Forest and cast EarthKing's Lieutenant, which will put a counter on Avatar Enthusiasts.\n\
\n\
Let me cast Avatar Enthusiasts.",
