    {
      "type": "llm_response",
      "player": "PilotA",
      "ts": "2026-09-20T02:46:01.546268-07:00",
      "seq": 41,
      "game_seq": 185,
      "reasoning": "I'm at 15 vs their 18, but their board is fully tapped from the attack — only June is untapped. Time to build my Ally board: Forest enables Earth King's Lieutenant, and I have exactly enough white left for Momo, which will trigger both Lieutenant and Avatar Enthusiasts.",
      "thinking": "Let me think about this turn. I'm at 15 life, opponent at 18. It's my turn 4 precombat main.\n\
\n\
My board: Avatar Enthusiasts 2/2, Island, Plains, Plains (3 lands untapped, land drop remaining).\n\
\n\
My hand: Earth King's Lieutenant {G}{W}, Earth Kingdom Soldier {4}{G/W}, Flexible Waterbender {3}{U}, Forest, Hakoda {3}{W}, Momo {W}, The Spirit Oasis {2}{U}.\n\
\n\
Opponent: Callous Inspector tapped, 2 Clues, Forest 4/4 land creature tapped, Forest tapped, June 2/2, Obsessive Pursuit, 2 Swamps tapped. 2 cards in hand.\n\
\n\
Options:\n\
1. Play Forest (land drop), then cast Earth King's Lieutenant for {G}{W} — puts a +1/+1 counter on Avatar Enthusiasts (making it 3/3), and Lieutenant gets bigger with future Allies. That leaves Island, Plains, Plains... wait, Forest would be my 4th land. Tapping Forest + Plains for Lieutenant leaves Island + Plains untapped = 2 mana, not enough for Momo ({W}) — actually Momo costs {W}, so I could cast Momo too! Lieutenant {G}{W} = Forest + Plains. Then Momo {W} = Plains. That leaves Island untapped.\n\
\n\
Wait, but casting Momo triggers Lieutenant (another Ally enters → Lieutenant gets +1/+1 counter) and Avatar Enthusiasts (another Ally enters → +1/+1 counter). So the sequence:\n\
- Lieutenant enters: puts +1/+1 counter on each other Ally I control → Avatar Enthusiasts becomes 3/3.\n\
- Momo enters: Lieutenant gets +1/+1 counter (becomes 2/2), Avatar Enthusiasts gets +1/+1 counter (becomes 4/4).\n\
\n\
That's a strong turn: 4/4 Avatar Enthusiasts, 2/2 Lieutenant, 1/1 Momo flier.\n\
\n\
Alternative: play The Spirit Oasis as land? No — it's a spell {2}{U} (an artifact/enchantment Shrine?). It says \"When this enters, draw a card for each Shrine you control.\" It would draw 0 (it counts other Shrines? \"for each Shrine you control\" — when it enters, does it count itself? It says \"Whenever another Shrine you control enters, draw a card\", so the ETB draw probably counts all Shrines including itself? Actually \"draw a card for each Shrine you control\" — when it enters, it's on the battlefield, so it counts itself → draw 1. But I don't have other Shrines. Better to play Forest and develop creatures.\n\
\n\
Earth King's Lieutenant first, then Momo. Board: Avatar 4/4, Lieutenant 2/2, Momo 1/1. That's great pressure.\n\
\n\
Attack? Avatar Enthusiasts doesn't have vigilance, but attacking with the team: opponent has June 2/2 (can't be blocked only if they've drawn 2 cards — blocking restriction applies to June as attacker, not blocker; as a blocker June is normal), Callous Inspector 1/1 menace (untapped next turn). Their 4/4 Forest creature — it's a land creature with haste; it's tapped this turn from attacking. On my turn it's untapped... wait, it tapped to attack on their turn, then untaps on their untap? No — creatures untap on their controller's untap step. They attacked on their turn 4, so it's tapped now during my turn 4? No wait, after their combat, they go to end step, then my turn begins. Their tapped creatures stay tapped until their next untap step. So Inspector and Forest 4/4 are tapped during my turn. Only June 2/2 is untapped as a potential blocker.\n\
\n\
If I attack with everything (Avatar 4/4, Lieutenant 2/2, Momo 1/1): June can block one. If June blocks Avatar (4/4), June dies, Avatar survives (takes 2). Trample? Lieutenant has trample. If June blocks Lieutenant, 1 trample damage goes through (2 power - 1 toughness = 1). Total damage: if June blocks Lieutenant: 4 (Avatar) + 1 (Momo) + 1 (trample) = 6 → opponent to 12. If June blocks Avatar: 2 + 1 = 3 → opponent to 15, June dies.\n\
\n\
But wait — Obsessive Pursuit: \"Whenever you attack, put X +1/+1 counters on target attacking creature, where X is the number of permanents you've sacrificed this turn.\" That's their attacking trigger, not relevant to mine.\n\
\n\
Should I attack? Avatar Enthusiasts 4/4 attacking — but I want to keep it back? Opponent's board: June 2/2, Inspector 1/1 menace, 4/4 land creature. Next turn they untap and can attack with the 4/4 land + others. Obsessive Pursuit gives counters when they attack based on permanents sacrificed (Clues). They have 2 Clues; if they sacrifice 2 Clues to draw, X=2... they could also sacrifice Inspector to June for another Clue. Hmm.\n\
\n\
I think attacking with Avatar Enthusiasts and Momo is good. Actually let's think: is there a reason to hold back? Their 4/4 Forest will be tapped on my turn regardless. Attacking puts pressure. If they block Avatar with June, June dies — good trade for me (June is their card advantage engine with Clue generation via sacrifice). Actually if June blocks Avatar 4/4, June dies and Avatar takes 2 damage becoming 4/2... no, Avatar is 4/4 with counters, takes 2 damage, survives. June dies. That's great.\n\
\n\
Hold Lieutenant back? Lieutenant is 2/2 with trample. Attacking with all: worst case June blocks Lieutenant, 1 tramples through, +4+1 = 6 damage. Good.\n\
\n\
Risk: opponent has 2 cards in hand — could have removal for Avatar. That's fine, I still get damage with others.\n\
\n\
Actually, should I even attack with Avatar Enthusiasts? It's my growing threat. If they have a removal spell they'd cast it anyway. Attacking is free-ish. But wait — if I attack with Avatar and they don't block, they take 4 → 18 to 14ish. Their life total is a resource; putting pressure matters because their Obsessive Pursuit drains them too.\n\
\n\
Let me sequence: play Forest, cast Earth King's Lieutenant (Forest + Plains), cast Momo (Plains). Then attack with Avatar Enthusiasts, Lieutenant, Momo. Island remains untapped (bluff Flexible Waterbender? No, I can't cast it with 1 Island... Flexible Waterbender costs {3}{U}, I don't have 4 mana. Island untapped does nothing but that's fine).\n\
\n\
Wait, actually should I hold Momo? No, casting Momo grows my board. Play it.\n\
\n\
Total mana: Forest + Plains + Plains + Island = 4 mana. Lieutenant {G}{W} uses Forest + Plains. Momo {W} uses Plains. Island left.\n\
\n\
First action: play Forest land.",
