      "reasoning": "They exiled my Avatar Enthusiasts with Sold Out — a big blow, but my life total matters more now. Blocking the 4/4 Forest with Momo saves 4 damage, and Momo's leaves-the-battlefield trigger still gives me value.",
      "thinking": "Let me analyze the current game state.\n\
\n\
My board:\n\
- 15 life\n\
- Hand: Earth Kingdom Soldier, Flexible Waterbender, Hakoda Selfless Commander, The Spirit Oasis\n\
- Battlefield: Earth King's Lieutenant 2/2 (summoning sick), Forest (tapped), Island, Momo Playful Pet 1/1 (summoning sick), Plains (tapped), Plains (tapped)\n\
- Exile: Avatar Enthusiasts (they exiled it with Sold Out!)\n\
\n\
Wait, Avatar Enthusiasts is in exile. The opponent used Sold Out on it after I attacked. That's why the chat says \"Had to take out the Enthusiasts!\"\n\
\n\
Opponent's board:\n\
- 12 life\n\
- 1 card in hand\n\
- Battlefield: Callous Inspector 1/1 (tapped, attacking), 3 Clue tokens, Forest 4/4 (tapped, attacking - this is the earthbent land from Earthbending Lesson), 2 more Forests (tapped), June Bounty Hunter 2/2, Obsessive Pursuit, 2 Swamps (tapped)\n\
- Graveyard: Earthbending Lesson, Sold Out\n\
\n\
Combat: Callous Inspector (1/1 menace) and Forest (4/4) are attacking me.\n\
\n\
I'm at 15. If I take both, that's 5 damage, putting me at 10.\n\
\n\
Blocking considerations:\n\
- Callous Inspector has menace, so I'd need two creatures to block it. I only have two creatures total (Earth King's Lieutenant and Momo), and they're both summoning sick... wait, can summoning sick creatures block? Yes! Summoning sickness only prevents attacking and activating tap abilities. Blocking is fine.\n\
\n\
- Earth King's Lieutenant is a 2/2. Momo is a 1/1 flyer.\n\
\n\
Options:\n\
1. Block the Forest 4/4 with Earth King's Lieutenant (2/2). My Lieutenant dies, Forest survives (takes 2, has 4 toughness). Bad trade - I lose my creature for nothing.\n\
\n\
2. Block the Forest with Momo (1/1). Momo dies, but Momo has a leaves-the-battlefield trigger: create a Food token, put a +1/+1 counter on target creature, or scry 2. If Momo dies, I can put a +1/+1 counter on Earth King's Lieutenant or scry 2. Momo dying to block 4 damage... I take 1 from Inspector instead of 4 from Forest. Net: I take 1 damage instead of 5, and Momo's death gives value (counter on Lieutenant or scry).\n\
\n\
Wait, but if I block Forest with Momo, Inspector still hits me for 1. I go to 14. Momo dies, and I get the leaves trigger. Actually, \"When this leaves the battlefield\" — so even dying works. I can put a +1/+1 counter on Earth King's Lieutenant making it a 3/3, or scry 2.\n\
\n\
3. Block Forest with Earth King's Lieutenant: Lieutenant dies, I take 1 from Inspector. Go to 14. But losing Lieutenant is worse than losing Momo I think. Lieutenant is a trampler that grows with each Ally.\n\
\n\
4. Don't block at all: take 5, go to 10.\n\
\n\
Let me think about the strategic picture. My Avatar Enthusiasts got exiled by Sold Out. That's a blow — it was a 5/5. Now my board is much weaker: 2/2 Lieutenant and 1/1 Momo.\n\
\n\
Opponent is at 12. They have June (2/2), Inspector (1/1), and a 4/4 earthbent Forest. Plus Obsessive Pursuit churning Clues.\n\
\n\
My hand: Earth Kingdom Soldier (4{G/W}, 3/4 vigilance, ETB puts counters on up to two creatures), Flexible Waterbender ({3}{U} 2/5 vigilance, waterbend to become 5/2), Hakoda ({3}{W} 3/5 vigilance, lets me cast Allies from top), The Spirit Oasis ({2}{U} Shrine, draws for each Shrine).\n\
\n\
My lands: Forest, Island, Plains, Plains — 4 lands. Next turn I can play Spirit Oasis (it's a land? Let me check: \"The Spirit Oasis {2}{U}: When this enters, draw a card for each Shrine you control.\" Hmm, the casting cost shown is {2}{U}, so it's a spell, not a land? Actually wait — in the card reference it shows \"The Spirit Oasis {2}{U}\" which suggests it's an enchantment or artifact with a mana cost. But the name \"The Spirit Oasis\" sounds like a land. Actually, looking at it, it has a mana cost {2}{U}, so it can't be a land (lands don't have mana costs). It's probably an enchantment — Shrine. So it costs 3 mana.\n\
\n\
Next turn I'll have 5 mana if I draw a land, or 4 mana with what I have. I can cast Earth Kingdom Soldier (5 mana: {4}{G/W}) if I draw a land, or Hakoda (4 mana: {3}{W}) or Flexible Waterbender ({3}{U}).\n\
\n\
Decision now: block or not?\n\
\n\
If I block the 4/4 Forest with Momo:\n\
- I take 1 (Inspector), go to 14.\n\
- Momo dies. Trigger: I can put a +1/+1 counter on Earth King's Lieutenant (making it 3/3) or scry 2.\n\
- The Forest is tapped and stays tapped... it survives.\n\
\n\
If I don't block:\n\
- I take 5, go to 10.\n\
\n\
Losing Momo vs taking 4 extra damage. Life total: going from 14 to 10 is significant. But opponent's board: Inspector 1/1, June 2/2, 4/4 Forest land. Their max damage per turn: 4+2+1 = 7 if everything attacks. At 10, I'd be in danger of dying in 2 turns. At 14, more comfortable.\n\
\n\
But Momo is my only flyer, and it's a 1/1. Its value going forward is modest. The death trigger gives value. I think blocking with Momo is right: save 4 life, get a counter or scry.\n\
\n\
Actually wait — should I consider blocking the Forest with Earth King's Lieutenant instead? If Lieutenant (2/2) blocks the 4/4, Lieutenant dies and deals 2 to the Forest (doesn't kill it). That's strictly worse than Momo blocking — I lose the bigger creature, and Momo's death at least triggers its leaves ability.\n\
\n\
Alternatively, block Inspector with both? Inspector has menace — I can block it with both Momo and Lieutenant. Then Inspector (1/1) deals 1 damage... it would kill one of them (1 damage to one blocker). Actually, attacker assigns damage: Inspector is 1/1, blocked by two creatures. It deals 1 damage to one of them (kill Momo 1/1 or deal 1 to Lieutenant). Meanwhile the blockers deal 2+1=3 to Inspector, killing it. When Inspector dies, \"it deals 1 damage to you. Create a Clue token.\" So I take 1 anyway, opponent gets a Clue.\n\
\n\
If I double-block Inspector with both:\n\
- Inspector dies, opponent gets a Clue, I take 1 from its death trigger.\n\
- Opponent chooses to kill either Momo or deal 1 to Lieutenant. They'd kill Momo (1 damage kills the 1/1). Then Momo's trigger gives me a counter on Lieutenant or scry.\n\
- Meanwhile the 4/4 Forest hits me for 4.\n\
\n\
Net: I take 4 (Forest) + 1 (Inspector death) = 5, go to 10. I lose Momo (get counter on Lieutenant, making it 3/3). Opponent loses Inspector but gets a Clue.\n\
\n\
Compare to blocking Forest with Momo:\n\
- I take 1, go to 14. Lose Momo (get counter on Lieutenant → 3/3 or scry). Forest survives.\n\
\n\
The first option kills Inspector but I take 5 total. The second saves my life total (14 vs 10) but leaves Inspector alive.\n\
\n\
Hmm, at 10 life vs 14 life. Their board without Inspector: June 2/2 + 4/4 Forest = 6 power. With Inspector: 7 power. \n\
\n\
Actually, let me reconsider: is killing Inspector worth 4 life and giving them a Clue? Inspector is a 1/1 menace that generates a Clue when it dies (for them) and pings me. Not a huge threat. The 4/4 Forest is the bigger threat.\n\
\n\
I think blocking the 4/4 Forest with Momo is best: I go to 14, Momo's trigger gives value (counter on Lieutenant → 3/3, or scry 2). Their 4/4 is tapped and doesn't die, but it's a land-creature; next turn it might be their only untapped threat... actually it'll untap normally.\n\
\n\
Wait, actually, one more consideration: does the Forest 4/4 have haste/trample? Earthbend gives haste. No trample. So Momo blocks all 4 damage. Good.\n\
\n\
Also, note the Forest is their land animated by Earthbending Lesson — \"When it dies or is exiled, return it to the battlefield tapped.\" If I could kill it, it comes back as a tapped land, which is actually fine for them. Not relevant now since I can't kill it with 1 power.\n\
\n\
So: block Forest with Momo. Then on Momo's leaves trigger, choose +1/+1 counter on Earth King's Lieutenant (makes it a 3/3 trampler) — that helps my board more than scry 2, I think. Actually, let me weigh: scry 2 helps find lands/gas. A 3/3 trample Lieutenant is a real threat. With Hakoda coming down and more Allies, the Lieutenant grows. I'll take the counter.\n\
\n\
Actually, wait. Let me reconsider whether to block at all. If I don't block, I go to 10. Their next turn: they can attack with June, Inspector, and the 4/4 Forest = 7 damage → I'd be at 3. Plus Obsessive Pursuit upkeep makes them lose 1 life and get a Clue. They could crack Clues for cards. That's very dangerous. At 14, after the same attack I'd be at 7. Much safer.\n\
\n\
Blocking with Momo is clearly correct. Lose a 1/1 flyer to save 4 life and get a counter or scry.\n\
\n\
Let me also send a chat message since it's been 2+ turns. Something like acknowledging their Sold Out play.\n\
\n\
Let me declare blockers: Momo blocks the Forest.\n\
\n\
blockers format: \"p40:p12\" (Momo blocks Forest).\n\
\n\
Also, Earth King's Lieutenant could ALSO block the Forest along with Momo? If both block the Forest: 2+1=3 damage to Forest (doesn't kill 4-toughness), Forest deals 4 damage split among blockers — opponent would kill both (assign 1 to Momo, 2 to Lieutenant... actually needs to assign lethal in order: they'd order and assign 1 to Momo (lethal), 2 to Lieutenant (lethal), 1 wasted). So both my creatures die, Forest survives with 3 damage. Terrible. No.\n\
\n\
Just Momo blocks Forest. Let me do that with a chat message.",
