      "reasoning": "Opponent cracked three Clues to grow June to a 5/5 with lifelink and swung with both creatures — but drawing 2+ cards means June is unblockable this turn. So the only sensible block is Katara on the Callous Inspector: she survives (3 toughness vs 1 power), kills it, and the Inspector's death trigger pings the opponent for 1. I take 5 from June and go to 9, but I keep both my creatures.",
      "thinking": "Wait — what happened? The opponent went down to 6? Let me parse. My Earth King's Lieutenant attacked, opponent blocked with June? No wait, June is at 5/5 with 3 counters. Hmm, opponent is at 6hp, and it's turn 6 COMBAT, opponent attacking me with Callous Inspector (1/1) and June (5/5). I'm at 14.\n\
\n\
Wait, what happened during the turns between? My Lieutenant attacked, opponent apparently didn't block (or blocked and took trample), going from 12 to 6 (took 5 damage, maybe with block by June the old June 2/2 died... but June is alive at 5/5). Actually opponent at 6 means they took 6 total more. Perhaps Lieutenant hit for 5 twice? No — it's turn 6 now, so my turn 5 attack hit for... they were at 12, now at 6: took 5 from Lieutenant (12→7), plus Obsessive Pursuit upkeep loss (7→6). That matches: unblocked 5 damage, then upkeep -1.\n\
\n\
Then opponent's turn 6: they played things, cashed Clues, June grew to 5/5 (3 counters from Obsessive Pursuit attack trigger, X=3 permanents sacrificed — they sacrificed 3 Clues). June now has lifelink from Obsessive Pursuit (X≥3 grants lifelink; June also has native lifelink per the text shown). They attack with Inspector and June.\n\
\n\
I'm at 14. If I take both: 1 + 5 = 6 damage → 8. They gain 5 life (lifelink) → 11. That's bad — big life swing.\n\
\n\
I have Katara 3/3 (sick — summoning sickness doesn't prevent blocking). I can block one attacker. June has lifelink and 5/5 — blocking June with Katara: Katara deals 3 to June, June deals 5 to Katara, Katara dies, opponent gains 5 life anyway. Blocking Inspector: 1/1 dies, opponent takes 1 from Inspector death trigger, I take 5 from June → 9, opponent gains 5 → 11, and opponent gets a Clue.\n\
\n\
