      "reasoning": null,
      "thinking": "I'm at 8 life. Opponent at 11. My board: Earth King's Lieutenant 7/7 trample, Hakoda 3/5 (sick), Katara 3/3. Opponent board: Callous Inspector 1/1 (tapped), June 5/5 (tapped), Forest 4/4 land (tapped), Clue token, all lands tapped.\n\
\n\
Opponent's entire board is tapped! June 5/5 tapped, Inspector tapped, Forest tapped. So no blockers at all. I attack with Lieutenant (7/7 trample) and Katara (3/3). That's 10 damage unblocked... opponent at 11, so they go to 1. Wait, 7+3 = 10, putting them at 1. Not lethal.\n\
\n\
Hmm, can I do better? Hakoda is summoning sick, can't attack. I have no untapped lands for a pump spell.\n\
\n\
Actually wait — could I attack with just both and deal 10, leaving them at 1? That's the best I can do this turn. Then they untap and June is unblockable and hits for 5, putting me at 3. Hmm, dangerous.\n\
\n\
But there's no choice to deal 11 this turn. Unless... no mana open. Earth Kingdom Soldier costs 5, I have 0 untapped lands. So attack with both for 10.\n\
\n\
Actually, should I consider not attacking with Katara to keep a blocker? Opponent's board is fully tapped; they'll untap on their turn regardless. June is unblockable when they draw 2 cards. Inspector has menace (needs 2 blockers). The 4/4 Forest... if I hold Katara back, she could block the Forest. But I'm at 8; if they attack with June (5, unblockable) + Forest (4) + Inspector (1 menace), blocking the Forest with Katara saves 4, I take 6, go to 2. If I don't block, I take 10 and die. So holding Katara back doesn't even save me if they attack with everything — actually blocking Forest: June unblockable 5 + Inspector menace 1 = 6, I'd be at 2. With Katara blocking, Katara 3/3 vs 4/4 Forest — Katara dies, Forest survives at... wait, the Forest is a 4/4, Katara 3/3 blocks, Forest takes 3 damage, survives; Katara dies.\n\
\n\
Alternatively, attack with both, opponent goes to 1. Then on their turn, Obsessive Pursuit upkeep: they lose 1 life and create a Clue. They die! Obsessive Pursuit says \"at the beginning of your upkeep, you lose 1 life and create a Clue token.\" So if I put them to 1, they lose 1 life at upkeep and die before doing anything.\n\
\n\
That's the line! Attack with both, deal 10, opponent at 1, then their upkeep trigger kills them. Unless they sacrifice Clues to... no, losing life isn't preventable. But wait, they could gain life? No lifegain on their board except Obsessive Pursuit attack trigger (needs to attack). At their upkeep, the trigger resolves and they lose 1 life, dying at 0.\n\
\n\
Unless they can respond to the trigger — the trigger goes on the stack at upkeep. They could sacrifice a creature to June? That doesn't gain life. They have no way to gain life at instant speed presumably. So attacking for 10 is lethal-on-upkeep.\n\
\n\
Even attacking with just the Lieutenant (7) puts them at 4 — not lethal. I need both attackers to get them to 1.\n\
\n\
So: attack with Earth King's Lieutenant and Katara. Hakoda is sick and can't anyway.\n\
\n\
Let me declare attackers.",
