        "pool_size": 2,
        "reasoning": "I'm drafting an Avatar: The Last Airbender set. My pool so far is UW (Aang, Swift Savior and Hakoda, Selfless Commander). So I'm in white-blue.\n\
\n\
Current pack options for my colors:\n\
- Flexible Waterbender {3}{U} - decent common, vigilance, can become 5/2\n\
- Bender's Waterskin {3} - mana rock that untaps during each other player's untap step, so it produces 4 mana per round in multiplayer... wait, this is a draft, presumably 1v1 games. Untaps during each other player's untap step - in a 2-player game, that's just normal untap. Hmm, actually \"during each other player's untap step\" means in two-player games it untaps normally (once per turn cycle). So it's a 3-mana mana rock that taps for any color. Decent for fixing, especially with my two-color pool and possibly splashing.\n\
- Octopus Form - combat trick, cheap\n\
- Otter-Penguin - weak\n\
- Waterbending Scroll {1}{U} - card draw artifact, uncommon. With islands it gets cheaper to activate.\n\
- The Spirit Oasis - Shrine synergy, I don't have shrines yet.\n\
- Rabaroo Troop {3}{W}{W} - double white, landfall, plainscycling.\n\
\n\
Best picks for UW: Waterbending Scroll is card advantage and cheap. Flexible Waterbender is a solid creature. Bender's Waterskin is fixing.\n\
\n\
In booster 1 pick 3, I want to stay on color. Waterbending Scroll seems strong - it's an uncommon that provides late-game card draw. But it's slow. Flexible Waterbender is a fine creature but commons are replaceable.\n\
\n\
Actually, Bender's Waterskin is colorless fixing which helps cast Aang (1WU) and Hakoda (3W). It taps for any color. In a 2-player game it untaps each turn cycle so it's basically a 3-mana rock that taps for any color—like a Mana Geode-ish. It also synergizes... nothing special.\n\
\n\
Waterbending Scroll: 1U artifact, {6}, {T}: Draw a card, costs {1} less for each Island. With 4 islands it's 2 mana to draw a card. That's quite good in a long game.\n\
\n\
I think Waterbending Scroll is the pick here—stays in blue, card advantage engine. Alternatively Flexible Waterbender for a solid body. Waterbend {3} makes it 5/2 vigilance... but it costs 3 to activate each turn.\n\
\n\
Given it's early in pack 1 and my pool is UW, I'll take Waterbending Scroll for the card advantage. Actually let me think again - removal and bombs win drafts. None here for my colors. Card draw is valuable.\n\
\n\
Alternatively, Bender's Waterskin is colorless and keeps me open, but I'm already committed to UW with two rares.\n\
\n\
I'll go with Waterbending Scroll (8).",
